# ===========================================================================
# data/ — deny-by-default for tabular data files
# ===========================================================================
# This is a second, local copy of the rule in the repository root .gitignore,
# deliberately duplicated. This directory is the one place in the project where
# licensed third-party corpus text lands, and the cost of a mistake here is a
# licence breach in a public repository. If someone edits or reorders the root
# file, this one still holds.
#
# Two of the three source corpora cannot be redistributed at all:
#   - Quora Question Pairs — Quora Terms of Service, no redistribution grant
#   - SODD                 — CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
# Every .csv and .tsv here is therefore ignored unless it is named below.
#
# Patterns in this file are relative to data/.
#
# To add an exception you must be able to state why the file is publishable:
# either it contains no third-party corpus text at all, or its text is
# synthetic and carries no upstream licence. If you cannot state that, it does
# not go on the list.

*.csv
*.tsv

# Update 2026-08-04 — extended beyond .csv/.tsv. `save_dataset()` writes the
# working dataset as CSV *and* JSON, so the .json half was protected by its
# exact filename alone; a raw shard copied out of raw/ was covered only while
# it stayed there.
*.json
*.parquet
*.parquet.gzip
*.data

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ allowed
# 15 synthetic fixture pairs. Fabricated text, source_corpus =
# "synthetic-fixture". No third-party licence. The offline test suite and the
# scripts/reproduce.sh defaults read this file.
!ground_truth.csv

# The published D2 artifact: identifiers and labels only. Carries pair_id,
# workload, source_corpus, source_pair_id, original_label, author_label and
# metadata — and no query text in any column, because DistributionRecord has no
# text fields. This is what a third party rehydrates from.
!ground_truth.ids.csv

# Added 2026-08-04: JSON twin of the fixtures, the provenance registry, and the
# sampling manifest. None carries query text.
!ground_truth.json
!corpora.json
!ground_truth.ids.meta.json
!annotation_progress.json

# ------------------------------------------------- deliberately NOT allowed
# Named here so the reasoning is on the record, not to add a rule — the
# blanket *.csv above already covers them:
#
#   ground_truth.full.csv        the rehydrated working dataset — full query
#                                text from all three corpora. Regenerate it
#                                with scripts/rehydrate_dataset.py; never
#                                commit it.
#   annotated-900.backup.csv     any hand-made backup or export of the working
#   *.backup.csv, *export*.csv   dataset carries exactly the same text.
#
# Anything under raw/ is already excluded by the root .gitignore
# (`data/raw/**`), which keeps the per-corpus directories but never their
# contents. See raw/README.md.
#
# Update 2026-08-04 — same for ground_truth.full.json, *.backup.json and
# *export*.json, now covered by *.json.
#
# Update 2026-08-06 — timestamped backups. Every write that would overwrite a
# ground-truth artifact copies the current file to backups/ first (see
# levy/dataset/backup.py), so this directory accumulates snapshots of
# ground_truth.full.{csv,json} — full corpus text — and of the ids file. The
# blanket *.csv / *.json rules above already cover them by extension; the
# directory is named explicitly because it is the one place in the project whose
# *contents* are unbounded and licence-bearing by design. Nothing in it is ever
# publishable, and nothing in it is ever deleted by the tooling.
backups/

# These rules are a staging filter only: `git add -f`, `git stash -u` and
# `git stash --all` all bypass them. `scripts/audit_release.sh` check 4 is the
# backstop — it scans `git log --all`, which includes refs/stash.
